## Why This Is Asked
Tests threat modeling and practical controls for log integrity across cloud boundaries, a common fintech risk.

## Key Concepts
- Log integrity, STRIDE/PASTA, SBOM, log signing, KMS, append-only storage, WORM, cross-cloud replication, SIEM/SOAR, tabletop exercises

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code for signing log entries
function signLogEntry(entry, key) {
  const signature = crypto.sign("SHA256", Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(entry)), key);
  return { entry, signature };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity of logs during audits across clouds?
- How would you coordinate key rotation and revocation in a distributed SIEM?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests crypto agility, cross-cloud governance, and practical CISSP controls for data at rest and in transit.

## Key Concepts
- Crypto agility and KMS key hierarchies across clouds
- Envelope encryption, per-tenant DEKs, field-level encryption
- Key rotation, revocation, auditability, incident response
- Data residency and edge deployment considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo rotation workflow
rotateMasterKey(cloud, keyId) {
  wrapNewDEKWithMasterKey(keyId);
  rewrapAllDataKeys();
  validateNoDowntime();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation impact on latency and availability?
- What would you monitor to detect key-compromise attempts and how would you respond?
